    {
      "course_code": "GLS",
      "course_num": "181",
      "course_combined": "GLS 181",
      "title": "General Learning Strategies II",
      "catalog_entry_url": "https://ssb.iit.edu/bnrprd/bwckctlg.p_disp_course_detail?cat_term_in=202720&subj_code_in=GLS&crse_numb_in=181",
      "course_description": "This course, based on our highly successful academic coaching model, is designed to create a pathway for students to excel in their studies in general and their early-stage college mathematics, which is a cornerstone for success in STEM degrees. Individualized Adaptive Learning (IAL; also known by the historical, but now less accurate, course series name, General Learning Strategies, GLS) 181 is a mentorship program that pairs you with MATH Peer Mentors. These mentors are trained in Empowerment, Leadership, and Mentorship (ELM) principles, are equipped with adaptive learning strategies, and have successfully navigated the challenges of college algebra, calculus, and beyond. Students who have completed their GLS courses have historically improved their overall semester GPA by more than a letter grade on average and continue to improve their academic performance.",
